Content:
Charter Communications (NASDAQ:CHTR) shares jumped after reports SpaceX discussed routing Starlink mobile traffic via Charter, fueling merger chatter after Comcast moves and a bond spike, even as analysts warn a nationwide wireless tie-up would need Verizon MVNO support and years of investment.

Previous Week Recap

• SpaceX Talks Boost Charter: CHTR stock surged after reports SpaceX held talks on a mobile tie-up. Intraday jump ~9%, premarket >24%. Reports say Starlink mobile may route traffic via Charter’s broadband; no deal announced.
• Analysts Mixed On CHTR Target: Goldman Sachs cut Charter Communications (CHTR) price target to $125 and kept a Sell; Citigroup and Bank of America kept Buy ratings. Traders: note target change and mixed analyst view.
• CHTR Q2 2026 Results Date: Charter Communications (CHTR) will release Q2 2026 results July 24 at 7:00 a.m. ET, followed by an 8:00 a.m. ET webcast; archived recording posted about two hours after the live event.
• Comcast Spin-Off Talks Boosts CHTR: CHTR 7% senior note due 2033 jumped ~4.125¢ after Comcast said it will spin off NBCUniversal and Sky, sparking market talk of a possible Comcast–Charter deal.
• Charter SpaceX Link Requires Verizon MVNO: Analysts say Charter (CHTR) linking with SpaceX would still rely on a Verizon MVNO deal, limiting nationwide wireless access; a standalone nationwide network would need years and huge capital.

