Content:
Sri Lankan shares fell on Monday, pulled down by losses in information technology stocks.

* The CSE All-Share index  settled 0.44% lower at 22,080.65 points, dropping for the fifth straight session

* SMB Finance PLC  and Softlogic Holdings PLC  were the top percentage losers on the index, down 10% and 8.7%, respectively, on the day.

* Trading volume on the index rose to 41.8 million shares from 30.6 million shares in the previous session.

* The equity market's turnover fell to 1.35 billion Sri Lankan rupees ($4.03 million) from 1.54 billion rupees in the previous session, according to exchange data.

* Foreign investors were net sellers, offloading stocks worth 332.7 million rupees, while domestic investors were net buyers, purchasing shares worth 1.34 billion rupees, the data showed.

* For a report on global markets, click

($1 = 334.9000 Sri Lankan rupees)
