Content:
Ondas completed the acquisition of High Point UAS through a Unit Purchase Agreement signed on Jul 02 2026. The consideration includes approximately $200 million in cash, with $12 million placed in escrow, 39,999,998 shares issued at closing, and 44,999,998 additional shares deliverable on Jan 4, 2027. In a related Registration Rights and Lock-Up Agreement, the Locked-Up Shares are restricted for six months post-closing, with 50% potentially locked for an additional six months if the 30-day average VWAP exceeds $20 before Jan 2, 2027. Sellers receive resale registration via prospectus supplements and face daily trading limits tied to 10% of average daily volume, designed to support an orderly market and reduce overhang.

Agreement 1: Ondas Acquires High Point UAS for $200 Million Cash Plus 85M Shares

• Agreement type: Unit Purchase Agreement (acquisition of High Point UAS)
• Counterparty: Highlander Partners Defense, DZYNE Management Holdings and High Flight (Sellers)
• Signed / Effective: Jul 02 2026 / same
• Reason: Expand UAS capabilities and defense market presence

Agreement 2: Ondas Grants Sellers Lock-Up and Resale Rights Following High Point UAS Deal

• Agreement type: Registration Rights and Lock-Up Agreement
• Counterparty: Sellers
• Signed / Effective: Jul 02 2026 / same
• Duration / Termination: 6 months initial; 50% may extend 6 more
• Reason: Manage share overhang and ensure orderly resale

Original SEC Filing: Ondas Inc. [ ONDS ] - 8-K - Jul. 06, 2026

