Overview

• US smart eyewear maker's preliminary Q2 net sales rose 71% yr/yr to $0.99 mln
• Growth led by Lucyd Armor smart safety eyewear
• Company secured initial Canadian retailer order and 50-store US retail test

Outlook

• Company expects expanded retail partnerships to drive revenue in H2 2026 and beyond
• Product deployment with Canadian retailer expected to begin in Q3 2026
• Company plans to launch Lucyd Aero smart eyewear collection in October 2026

Result Drivers

• LUCYD ARMOR DEMAND - Growth led by sustained demand for Lucyd Armor smart safety eyewear across direct-to-consumer, online marketplace, and wholesale channels
• NEW RETAIL PARTNERSHIPS - Secured initial order from leading Canadian optical retail group and 50-store test with major U.S. retailer
• RETAIL STRATEGY EXPANSION - Accelerating wholesale and brick-and-mortar retail strategy expected to drive future revenue

