Content:
Italy's Treasury said on Monday it had mandated a pool of banks to sell a new three-tranche U.S. dollar-denominated BTP via syndication.

The bonds are due on July 14, 2031, 2036 and 2056, the Treausry said in a statement.

The deal will be launched in the near future, subject to market conditions.

BofA, Citigroup, Goldman Sachs and Morgan Stanley will manage the issuance, the Treasury added.
