Content:
San Francisco, United States, July 6th, 2026, Chainwire

A multi-agent AI review of Clouded’s bonding-curve attention market, more than 1,200 lines of Solidity across six contracts, delivered in hours.

Cecuro, the leading agentic smart contract auditing platform ranked #1 on OpenAI’s exploit benchmark, has completed a security audit of Clouded, an attention market built on HyperEVM. The review covered Clouded’s full six-contract suite, more than 1,200 lines of Solidity, including its bonding-curve market engine, staking DAO, and multisignature treasury. Clouded lets traders use  to take positions on social sentiment rather than settled outcomes, a design that falls outside standard prediction-market audit patterns.

Cecuro examined the complete Clouded codebase written in Solidity version 0.8.24. Scope included the core market contract, which issues positions as ERC1155 tokens priced along a bonding curve where cost rises as more shares are purchased; the CloudedDAO module that handles staking, revenue distribution, and market blacklisting; the CloudedPoint epoch-based rewards system; a multisignature treasury wallet; and the ERC20 governance and founder tokens. Cecuro’s multi-agent system reasons about each contract from several independent perspectives, then validates every candidate issue with a proof-of-concept exploit before it reaches the final report. The engagement was completed in hours rather than the weeks typical of manual review.

Attention and prediction markets have drawn heavy on-chain volume through the last market cycle, and novel mechanism designs concentrate risk in code that has no established audit template. Bonding-curve pricing, epoch reward accounting, and multisignature treasury logic each introduce failure modes that generic tooling and pattern matching tend to miss. HyperEVM, an emerging execution environment, adds a further layer of contracts that have not yet accumulated the battle testing of older chains. Independent review before mainnet exposure remains the practical way for teams in this category to reduce that risk.

“Attention markets break the assumptions most audit playbooks are built on, because there is no external oracle settling a position and value moves entirely through the curve and the reward accounting,” said Daniel, CEO at Cecuro. “That is exactly where reasoning from multiple angles pays off. Our agents do not just scan for known signatures. They model how a trader, a market creator, and a DAO staker each interact with the same contract, then try to break the invariants that hold the system together.”

The founder of Clouded, Ruo Yan, pointed to the workflow rather than any single result. “I’ve been using Cecuro to audit Clouded, and the thing that stands out most is that it shows you invalid findings alongside the real ones, which sounds minor, but it genuinely helps you understand your code better. It also caught issues that slipped through the other AI auditors I had used. The re-audit cycle is also a nice touch. You submit fixes and run it again, so it fits into your actual development process rather than just being a one-time report.”

The audit report has been delivered to the Clouded team for remediation and disclosure at their discretion. Clouded’s markets are accessible through its application, and protocol details are available at their website. Cecuro continues to review protocols across all major networks and smart contract languages. Teams preparing for launch can start a review, including a free audit scan at https://cecuro.ai

About Cecuro

Cecuro an agentic smart-contract auditing platform that ranks #1 on OpenAI’s exploit benchmark, EVMBench, and has a track record of finding vulnerabilities that top audit firms miss. Each security scan is done in hours, not weeks, at roughly 90 percent lower cost than traditional audits. Its proprietary multi-agent AI system reasons about contracts from multiple perspectives and validates each finding with proof-of-concept exploits before reporting. Cecuro supports all blockchain networks and smart-contract languages, with a free trial included.

To learn more about Cecuro, users can visit https://cecuro.ai.

Contact

CEO

Daniel Delouya

Cecuro

daniel@cecuro.ai
