Content:
Polish pipeline operator Gaz-System said no market participants reserved additional capacity at an auction on the Poland-Ukraine interconnection on Monday.

Gaz-System announced in May that it would offer additional transmission capacity for long-term gas exports to Ukraine at the auction, and that a successful auction would give grounds for investment in additional export capacity.

"No market participants reserved incremental capacity in the annual auction on the Poland-Ukraine interconnection, therefore the economic test was negative on both sides of the Polish-Ukrainian border," Gaz-System said in a statement.

"In this case... the process of obtaining incremental capacity is terminated."

The next assessment of demand is planned for July 2027.
